    {
      "image": "videos/07-future-self-stranger/2.jpg",
      "seconds": 18.81,
      "text": "Hal Hershfield put people in a scanner and asked them to think about themselves today, themselves in ten years, and a complete stranger. There is a region that quiets down when you think about someone who is not you. For many people, thinking about their future self quieted it the same way. And the bigger that gap, the less they saved for retirement.",
      "delivery": {
        "rate": 12,
        "pitch": 0
      },
      "clips": [
        {
